1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,281
DRISHTI blinks seasons apart —
watch the middle, a dot moves.

2
00:00:10,281 --> 00:00:23,933
Hand-blinks don't scale — six of eight,
this field's cached epochs, in a browser.

3
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:32,360
Ninety-six years ago —
Tombaugh, Pluto, at Lowell.

4
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:39,438
Same trick, built to scale, on your phone.

5
00:00:39,438 --> 00:00:45,000
DRISHTI blinks it in the browser.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,925
SPHEREx tints by spot.

7
00:00:47,925 --> 00:00:52,844
Six LVF wedges, hundred-two channels.

8
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:56,567
Tile 2 bluer, Tile 5 redder.

9
00:00:58,067 --> 00:00:59,928
The tint trap.

10
00:00:59,928 --> 00:01:01,258
Same star.

11
00:01:01,258 --> 00:01:04,050
Can't fairly compare.

12
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:12,426
Tombaugh blinked matched plates;
ours switch filters mid-blink.

13
00:01:12,426 --> 00:01:18,409
Same tint only — the
rest waits on the shelf.

14
00:01:18,409 --> 00:01:27,982
Nothing deleted for this question;
older versions stay listed on screen.

15
00:01:27,982 --> 00:01:32,901
Archive intact, waiting, ready still.

16
00:01:32,901 --> 00:01:42,208
Good data, idle, intact — while real
change could slip past unnoticed.

17
00:01:42,208 --> 00:01:45,000
That's the tint rule.

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,078
A visitor from another star.

19
00:01:48,078 --> 00:01:49,397
Stare loses.

20
00:01:49,397 --> 00:01:53,464
Follow Horizons path, visit by visit.

21
00:01:53,464 --> 00:01:55,663
3I/ATLAS, C/2025 N1.

22
00:01:55,663 --> 00:01:57,311
SPHEREx image —

23
00:01:57,311 --> 00:02:00,169
Gaia stars, Horizons path.

24
00:02:01,569 --> 00:02:05,856
Faint — tracked frame to tracked frame.

25
00:02:05,856 --> 00:02:12,012
Blinked, not subtracted — the
gray Diff is display-only.

26
00:02:12,012 --> 00:02:13,441
We messed up.

27
00:02:14,441 --> 00:02:17,299
Pre-fix flagged a control.

28
00:02:17,299 --> 00:02:19,937
Flagged pixels, not sky.

29
00:02:19,937 --> 00:02:23,565
Verdict withdrawn — "can't tell."

30
00:02:23,565 --> 00:02:29,281
For 3I: six bands, twenty
of twenty cutouts tracked.

31
00:02:29,281 --> 00:02:33,898
Transient IBE 503s retried, all recovered.

32
00:02:33,898 --> 00:02:36,756
None hollow, never joined.

33
00:02:36,756 --> 00:02:45,000
Faint — no outburst detected at these
uncertainties; slower change allowed.

34
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,823
A classroom with no wifi can blink
this field's cached epochs offline.

35
00:02:52,823 --> 00:03:00,087
One hundred forty-three epochs
across twenty fields, public JSON.

36
00:03:00,087 --> 00:03:02,098
No login to blink.

37
00:03:02,098 --> 00:03:06,121
We cached it so planes stay offline.

38
00:03:06,121 --> 00:03:07,462
Code is MIT.

39
00:03:07,462 --> 00:03:10,256
Scan that QR when online.

40
00:03:10,256 --> 00:03:15,397
A question stays open —
census-wide agreement.

41
00:03:15,397 --> 00:03:18,414
Prove us wrong, we'll post.

42
00:03:18,414 --> 00:03:20,985
Tonight: blink a field.

43
00:03:20,985 --> 00:03:26,125
File two epochs to Issues,
login only to file.

44
00:03:26,125 --> 00:03:29,701
Pass or fail, we read every one.

45
00:03:29,701 --> 00:03:33,836
Tombaugh blinked plates into history.

46
00:03:33,836 --> 00:03:43,000
We blink one hundred forty-three epochs
across twenty fields, recheckable as data.
